[[:db/retract 17592186124949 :question/answer-fields 17592186122294] [:db/retract 17592186124779 :question/answer-fields 17592186121271] {:db/id 17592186124227 :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations: \n![](images/25/25201f6dcb40f679ff8cb1a6f2effd1018816a614476f9355076eee8edf14d21.svg)\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124228 :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n![](images/7e/7e489d8b5dd4a2b8fde454dc57a91b0f0a28049c96b27ef76e9198f4967cb84d.svg)\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5-t \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-t \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nThis implies that the line passes through the point $(5,3,1)$ and is parallel to the vector ![](images/80/80cf9513aeb2ab2f87dda54ca16cdab76ff55024be1f7822fc9d1434b62382de.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124230 :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-t \\\\ 9t \\\\ -7t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-t \\\\ -5+9t \\\\ 3-7t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t \\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overline{PQ}$ are the following:\n![](images/48/4806a3eda16324e3216e0b21d4006daa37dedc7a36741c0bd2919b7eafccb05d.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124779 :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3t-12 \\\\ y=-5-7t \\\\ z=\\frac{3}{4}t+\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3t-12 \\\\ -5-7t \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}t+\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ -7t \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-12,-5,\\frac{1}{5})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-82f02e4f-8fa1-5737-a974-c8725a5027aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-82f02e4f-8fa1-5737-a974-c8725a5027aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "82f02e4f-8fa1-5737-a974-c8725a5027aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0df5346d-2966-5621-a5f7-4d0c104072b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3399bc79-2b67-5b83-87af-7604a8fccdc9" "answer-e0cb3c90-da08-5155-bc03-351fcfe80179" "answer-bad600d9-2cbf-50b7-ab3f-443e1558ed42" "answer-0df5346d-2966-5621-a5f7-4d0c104072b0" "answer-477dde1b-8255-51b0-8585-d23e885143e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3399bc79-2b67-5b83-87af-7604a8fccdc9" :answer/id #uuid "3399bc79-2b67-5b83-87af-7604a8fccdc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -7 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0cb3c90-da08-5155-bc03-351fcfe80179" :answer/id #uuid "e0cb3c90-da08-5155-bc03-351fcfe80179" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bad600d9-2cbf-50b7-ab3f-443e1558ed42" :answer/id #uuid "bad600d9-2cbf-50b7-ab3f-443e1558ed42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0df5346d-2966-5621-a5f7-4d0c104072b0" :answer/id #uuid "0df5346d-2966-5621-a5f7-4d0c104072b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-477dde1b-8255-51b0-8585-d23e885143e2" :answer/id #uuid "477dde1b-8255-51b0-8585-d23e885143e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125899 :tutorial/content "Suppose that we have a straight line passing through the point $P(3,-1,7)$ and that's parallel to the direction vector ![](images/54/54405c5c6e2502e5174525c2ee36a99366a79933b47e316a09858f827fda8dae.svg) As we know, we can write the vector equation of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nUsing the vector equation above, we can create a set of **parametric equations** where we express a general point $(x,y,z)$ in terms of  the parameter $t.$\n\nIf we let ![](images/67/67b8360f90540ffb75d39717c375f0ef6e9a8a39cae5832c78957105e0d148b6.svg) be the position vector of the general point $(x,y,z),$ then the above equation can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1+5t \\\\ 7-3t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n![](images/64/64cf325014eff341673557321ef565e35988b836630f3fbeb52af8024d7aaad7.svg)\n\nThe equations in the above system are called the **parametric equations** of the straight line.\nGeometrically, the equation states that a point belongs to the line if and only if its coordinates have the form\n\n$$\n(3, \\: -1+5t, \\: 7-3t),\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty, \\infty).$\n\n![](images/e2/e29ce95cdccb47b97578f6431a96e608f7af9f6709410b221ff517b436896608.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124717 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
